.TH HD-BACKUP-LOAD 8 "October 2026" "hd-backup" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-backup-load, hd-backup-unload \- connect and disconnect a backup drive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-backup-load
.I pool
.br
.B hd-backup-unload
.I pool
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-backup-load
imports the ZFS pool
.I pool
of a backup drive made with
.BR hd\-backup\-prep (8),
asks for its passphrase and mounts it, at
.IR /mnt/pool .
It imports with
.BR "zpool import \-f" ,
so a drive that was not unloaded, because it was pulled or the system went
down, can be loaded again.
.PP
.B hd-backup-unload
exports the pool, which unmounts it and forgets its key, so the drive can be
disconnected.
.PP
Run them as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLE
.RS
.nf
sudo hd-backup-load bk01
hd-backup write home /mnt/bk01
sudo hd-backup-unload bk01
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when a step fails, 130 when it is interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd\-backup (1),
.BR hd\-backup\-prep (8),
.BR zpool\-import (8),
.BR zpool\-export (8),
.BR zfs\-load\-key (8)
